'' AN ENUM CONSTANT PASSED BYREF IS A TEMPORARY HOLDING ITS VALUE. AddrOfVar refused a
'' 'const' but not an enum member, so LowerAddr minted a frame slot named after the
'' member -- 'local i64 e_b; call void PU(@e_b)' -- that nothing ever stored to: the
'' callee read 0, and through a generic container's 'byref v as T' Push, stack garbage.
'' fbc passes a temporary, as for a literal. Output measured with fbc-modern 1.20
'' (2026-10-11); fbc warns 5 (implicit conversion) at PD, tiko does not.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/mir/src/enum-const-byref-run.bas -o tests/mir/enumconstbyrefrun.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/mir/enumconstbyrefrun.exe
'' RUN: tests/mir/enumconstbyrefrun.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ulong:6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: long: 6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: integer: 6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: enum: 6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: byte: 5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: double: 6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: long: 6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: long: 41
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: bumped: 105
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: after: 5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: box:56 2
